Let $P(x) = a_{10} x^{10} + a_9 x^9 + a_8 x^8 + \dots + a_2 x^2 + a_1 x + a_0.$ The roots of $P(x) = 0$ are $r_1, r_2, \dots, r_{10},$ which are integers.
We are also given that the polynomial $Q(x) = a_0 x^{10} + a_1 x^9 + a_2 x^8 + \dots + a_8 x^2 + a_9 x + a_{10}$ has the same roots $r_1, r_2, \dots, r_{10}.$
By Vieta's formulas, we have
\begin{align*} \sum_{i=1}^{10} r_i &= -\frac{a_9}{a_{10}} \\ \sum_{1 \le i < j \le 10} r_i r_j &= \frac{a_8}{a_{10}} \\ \dots \\ r_1 r_2 \dots r_{10} &= (-1)^{10} \frac{a_0}{a_{10}} = \frac{a_0}{a_{10}} \end{align*}
Also, since $r_1, r_2, \dots, r_{10}$ are the roots of $Q(x),$ by Vieta's formulas,
\begin{align*} \sum_{i=1}^{10} r_i &= -\frac{a_1}{a_0} \\ \sum_{1 \le i < j \le 10} r_i r_j &= \frac{a_2}{a_0} \\ \dots \\ r_1 r_2 \dots r_{10} &= (-1)^{10} \frac{a_{10}}{a_0} = \frac{a_{10}}{a_0} \end{align*}
Then we have
\begin{align*} -\frac{a_9}{a_{10}} &= -\frac{a_1}{a_0} \\ \frac{a_8}{a_{10}} &= \frac{a_2}{a_0} \\ \dots \\ \frac{a_0}{a_{10}} &= \frac{a_{10}}{a_0} \end{align*}

